body:
FYI this bug is currently happening in vue 3.2.47. I am simply running the `vite --host` command.

Given the shortened following component:

```html
<template>
    <Icon :icon="icon" />
</template>

<script setup lang="ts">
import { computed, toRefs } from 'vue'

const props = defineProps<{
  state: 'pending' | 'running' | 'completed' | 'failed'
}>()

const { bgColor, color, icon } = toRefs(useStatusDisplay(state))
</script>

<style scoped lang="scss">
.run-status :deep(i) {
  color: v-bind(color);
}
</style>
```

it outputs

```ts
setup(__props, { expose }) {
    expose();
    const props = __props;
    _useCssVars((_ctx) => ({
      "1c89043a-color": _unref(color)
    }));
    const { bgColor, color, icon } = toRefs(useStatusDisplay(state));
}
```

with the error: `Uncaught (in promise) ReferenceError: Unhandled Promise Rejection: can't access lexical declaration 'color' before initialization`

@Lyokolux 
It can work normally because this code will run after mounting.
```js
(_ctx) => ({
	"1c89043a-color": _unref(color)
})
```
it works fine see [demo](https://play.vuejs.org/#__DEV__eNpNj8HKwjAQhF9lyaUV/C1e/VPBV/CcS01WG0iTkGwLUvrubtoi5pQdZr6dncUtxtM0orgISThE1xFelQd+0tgJtOtybpXoz0rsOkBvy082bGBNNj9BHrNONhJkpDGC6/yL45TXuB1iSAQz6DDEkdAcIWGnyU54BAp3fGZY4JnCABWXqgqPvT4zjngBtF9/PevgQrpUCU21HJTfbAXNMlPaHVivSTbIZmu2t6S3Q8g6RDTA0qk/w1zO2rAw/T2sN/U6Hf6VX1ZACV3F8gFqn2uu)
Would you mind provide a runnable mimimal reproduction?
